WEBVTT

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.392
the excimer laser robotically sculpts the
exposed corneal bed

00:03:33.392 --> 00:03:34.952
into the correct shape.

00:03:34.952 --> 00:03:40.641
This process usually takes less than 30 
seconds for each eye.

00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:42.451
Finally, the flap is closed,

00:03:42.451 --> 00:03:46.341
and its edges reseal themselves 
in just a few hours.

00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:49.951
Because the lasering is done on 
the eyeball itself,

00:03:49.951 --> 00:03:53.357
it’s described as “in situ,” or “on site.”

00:03:53.357 --> 00:03:57.543
Its complete name is “laser in-situ 
keratomileusis” –

00:03:57.543 --> 00:04:00.553
but you probably know it as LASIK.